A battery is connected to two resistors $X$ and $Y$, as shown in Fig. 6.1.

{{figure:9702_s22_21_q06_figure_6_1}}

The resistance of resistor $X$ is greater than the resistance of resistor $Y$.

A battery of electromotive force (e.m.f.) $9.0\text{ V}$ and negligible internal resistance is connected in series with a light-dependent resistor (LDR) and a fixed resistor of resistance $1800\,\Omega$, as shown in Fig. 6.2.

{{figure:9702_s22_21_q06_figure_6_2}}

A voltmeter is connected across the fixed resistor. The reading on the voltmeter is $5.4\text{ V}$.
